1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,358
You press play in Mumbai.

2
00:00:02,358 --> 00:00:04,940
The video lives on a server in Virginia.

3
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:07,784
That is almost thirteen thousand kilometres away.

4
00:00:07,984 --> 00:00:09,881
Even at the speed of light in fibre,

5
00:00:09,881 --> 00:00:11,914
the round trip takes over a tenth of a

6
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:12,570
second.

7
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:15,900
Amazon CloudFront exists to shorten that trip.

8
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:17,637
The idea is simple.

9
00:00:17,637 --> 00:00:19,379
Do not make the file travel.

10
00:00:19,379 --> 00:00:21,291
Put a copy near the viewer.

11
00:00:21,491 --> 00:00:22,677
In two thousand eight,

12
00:00:22,677 --> 00:00:25,957
CloudFront launched with fourteen of these locations.

13
00:00:26,157 --> 00:00:28,571
Today there are more than six hundred points of

14
00:00:28,571 --> 00:00:30,554
presence, in over a hundred cities.

15
00:00:31,304 --> 00:00:33,464
Here is the journey of one request.

16
00:00:33,464 --> 00:00:36,260
Your phone asks DNS where the file lives.

17
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,714
DNS answers with a nearby edge location,

18
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:41,082
the one that should be fastest for you.

19
00:00:41,282 --> 00:00:43,041
The edge checks its cache.

20
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:44,381
If the file is there,

21
00:00:44,381 --> 00:00:45,219
that is a hit,

22
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:46,558
and you are done.

23
00:00:46,758 --> 00:00:47,502
If it is not,

24
00:00:47,502 --> 00:00:48,412
that is a miss.

25
00:00:48,412 --> 00:00:50,811
The edge asks a regional edge cache,

26
00:00:50,811 --> 00:00:52,880
a bigger shelf one layer up.

27
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:56,157
Still nothing? Only then does the request travel all

28
00:00:56,157 --> 00:00:57,624
the way to the origin.

29
00:00:57,824 --> 00:00:59,717
The origin sends the file back,

30
00:00:59,717 --> 00:01:02,315
and every layer on the way keeps a copy.

31
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,662
The next viewer in Mumbai gets a hit.

32
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:07,065
And if a thousand people ask at once,

33
00:01:07,065 --> 00:01:10,109
CloudFront merges them into a single request to the

34
00:01:10,109 --> 00:01:10,784
origin.

35
00:01:11,534 --> 00:01:13,968
Each copy stays fresh for a set time.

36
00:01:13,968 --> 00:01:16,819
When it expires, the edge checks again.

37
00:01:17,019 --> 00:01:18,430
The origin works less.

38
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:20,090
The viewer waits less.

39
00:01:20,290 --> 00:01:22,666
The video was never really in Virginia.

40
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:24,401
It was already next door.
